{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/561563-origins-what-s-the-point","id":561563,"title":"Origins... what's the point?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-19T22:07:32-07:00","id":561563,"title":"Origins... what's the point?","content":"Okay, inflammatory title aside, Back when WW announced the World of Darkness Core Book everyone was like &quot;Neat, the rules will be in one place&quot; or &quot;DAMMIT I DON'T WANNA BUY TWO BOOKS!&quot;. Either way, when I got both it and Requiem in the mail I remember skimming through Requiem in awe of the art and the feel and the shiny new clans and then, when I wanted to know how stuff worked I put it down and picked up the Core Book.<br /> <br /> By the time I put it down I had already decided to put my impending Vampire game on hold for what turned out to be a 9 month World of Darkness game. It was JUST. THAT. COOL.<br /> <br /> So now we're getting Origin. Its the Core Book for Scion, a big book of rules for the whole system... but what is it ABOUT?<br /> <br /> Is it a World of Brightness filled with Miracles just waiting to be discovered by unvisited Scions? Are their cults selling Minotaur Hormones to desperate college athletes? What are we doing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T00:06:02-07:00","id":561645,"title":"","content":"From what Joe Carriker said when he was developing it, Origins was being made with an eye to being an urban fantasy RPG, taking inspiration from everything from the Dresden Files to the books of Charles de Lint, and offering inspiration for playing in a world seeing Legend rise once more and how that affects normal people.<br /> <br /> Joe indicated there'd be a core of setting-agnostic stuff, as with Hero 1e, and some settings to plop characters down in.<br /> <br /> Neall indicates there'll be a base setting with the involvement of possibilities for alternate settings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T00:07:26-07:00","id":561647,"title":"","content":"It's a chance to play in a straight urban fantasy game. Like mythology it will be all shades of dark and light, because myths are full of wonder, but also very not nice at the same time.<br /> <br /> It's a stepping stone for pre-visitation Scions to learn about their world, as well as flushing out all of the ways the mythical exists all around them.<br /> <br /> Like all of Scion, it's about characters getting caught up in myths and doing awesome stuff. Whether you keep it at Origin tier the whole time because that's cool, or move on to Hero and beyond later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T09:13:55-07:00","id":561990,"title":"","content":"Very cool. I remember hearing the &quot;urban fantasy&quot; bit, I should have remembered it. Thanks, guys.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}